# Traffic Violation Detection System - Implementation Plan

## Overview
Enhance TAVISO to detect traffic violations using YOLOv11 + DeepSORT + PaddleOCR. Display webcam/IP camera on the left, real-time violations on the right, and violation history at bottom-right.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Confirmed Requirements:**
> - Camera on left, realtime violations on right, file storage bottom-right
> - PaddleOCR for license plate reading
> - Save to both CSV and SQLite database
> - Display: Date, Time (hour:minute), License Plate for each violation
> - No GPIO/firmware needed

---

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Backend Services

#### [MODIFY] [detector.py](file:///a:/TAVISO/backend/services/detector.py)
- Use YOLOv11 to detect vehicles AND license plates
- Replace EasyOCR with PaddleOCR (better Vietnamese support)
- Keep existing structure, update OCR implementation

```python
from paddleocr import PaddleOCR
ocr = PaddleOCR(use_angle_cls=True, lang='en', use_gpu=False)
result = ocr.ocr(plate_image, cls=True)
```

---

#### [NEW] [violation_detector.py](file:///a:/TAVISO/backend/services/violation_detector.py)
Detect violations and combine with license plate:
- Wrong-way driving detection
- Line crossing detection
- Speed estimation
- Return: `{violation_type, license_plate, timestamp, confidence}`

---

#### [MODIFY] [tracker.py](file:///a:/TAVISO/backend/services/tracker.py)
- Enhanced trajectory analysis
- Add speed calculation, line crossing detection

---

### 2. Database & Storage

#### [MODIFY] [models.py](file:///a:/TAVISO/backend/models.py)
New TrafficViolation model:
```python
class TrafficViolation(Base):
    id: int
    license_plate: str       # "43A-12345"
    violation_type: str      # "wrong_way", "speeding"
    timestamp: datetime      # Full datetime
    confidence: float
    speed_kmh: float         # Optional
    image_path: str          # Screenshot
```

---

#### [MODIFY] [logger.py](file:///a:/TAVISO/backend/services/logger.py)
Update to save both:
- **SQLite**: `data/database/violations.db`
- **CSV**: `data/csv/violations.csv`

CSV format:
```csv
id,license_plate,violation_type,date,time,confidence,speed_kmh
1,43A-12345,wrong_way,2026-01-15,12:30:45,0.85,
2,43B-67890,speeding,2026-01-15,12:35:22,0.92,55
```

---

### 3. API Endpoints

#### [MODIFY] [main.py](file:///a:/TAVISO/backend/main.py)
New endpoints:
- `GET /api/violations` - List violations (paginated)
- `GET /api/violations/stats` - Statistics
- `GET /api/violations/realtime` - Latest 10 violations for realtime display

---

### 4. Frontend

#### [MODIFY] [index.html](file:///a:/TAVISO/frontend/index.html)
Layout:
```
+---------------------------+--------------------+
|                           | Thống kê vi phạm   |
|   CAMERA STREAM           | (realtime)         |
|   (BÊN TRÁI)              +--------------------+
|                           | Lịch sử lưu trữ    |
|                           | (file CSV/DB)      |
+---------------------------+--------------------+
```

Realtime table columns:
| Ngày | Giờ | Biển số | Loại vi phạm |
|------|-----|---------|--------------|
| 15/01/2026 | 12:30 | 43A-12345 | Đi ngược chiều |

---

### 5. Configuration

#### [MODIFY] [settings.yaml](file:///a:/TAVISO/config/settings.yaml)
```yaml
camera:
  source: 0  # 0=webcam, or rtsp://ip:port/stream

violation:
  enable_wrong_way: true
  enable_speeding: true
  speed_limit_kmh: 40
  
storage:
  csv_path: "data/csv/violations.csv"
  db_path: "data/database/violations.db"
  save_images: true
  images_dir: "data/images"
```

---

### 6. Requirements

#### [MODIFY] [requirements.txt](file:///a:/TAVISO/requirements.txt)
Keep paddlepaddle and paddleocr for license plate reading.

